  "before_interfaces": {
    "def-ip-nonlinear-forward-map": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be real Hilbert spaces and let $U\\subseteq X$ be a nonempty open set in the norm topology. A **nonlinear forward model on Hilbert spaces** is a map $F:U\\to Y$; no linearity is assumed, and linear maps are allowed as special cases. For $y\\in Y$, its exact solution set is\n\n$$S_F(y):=\\{x\\in U:F(x)=y\\}.$$\n\nA point $x^\\dagger\\in U$ generates the exact datum $y=F(x^\\dagger)$. When $F$ is Fréchet differentiable at $x\\in U$, write $F'(x):X\\to Y$ for its unique bounded real-linear derivative."
    ],
    "def-ip-x0-minimum-norm-solution": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $U\\subseteq X$ be a nonempty open set, let $F:U\\to Y$ be a forward map, let $y\\in Y$, and let $x_0\\in X$. A point $x^\\dagger\\in U$ is an **$x_0$-minimum-norm solution** of $F(x)=y$ on $U$ if $F(x^\\dagger)=y$ and\n\n$$\\|x^\\dagger-x_0\\|\\le\\|x-x_0\\|\\qquad\\text{for every }x\\in U\\text{ with }F(x)=y.$$\n\nThis definition asserts no existence or uniqueness; it describes the minimizing property of a supplied exact solution. The minimum is global over the exact solution set on $U$, with distance measured from the specified reference point $x_0$."
    ],
    "def-ip-tangential-cone-condition": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $U\\subseteq X$ be open, and let $F:U\\to Y$ be Fréchet differentiable at $x\\in U$. For $\\delta>0$ such that the closed ball\n\n$$\\overline B_\\delta(x):=\\{x+h:h\\in X,\\ \\|h\\|_X\\le\\delta\\}$$\n\nis contained in $U$, the **local tangential cone condition at $x$ on radius $\\delta$ with constant $\\eta$** holds if $0\\le\\eta<1$ and\n\n$$\\|F(x+h)-F(x)-F'(x)h\\|_Y\\le\\eta\\,\\|F(x+h)-F(x)\\|_Y\\qquad(\\|h\\|_X\\le\\delta).$$"
    ],
    "lem-ip-tcc-residual-derivative-comparison": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $U\\subseteq X$ be open, and let $F:U\\to Y$ be Fréchet differentiable at $x\\in U$. Suppose that for some $\\delta>0$ with $\\overline B_\\delta(x)\\subseteq U$ and some $0\\le\\eta<1$, the local tangential cone condition at $x$ holds on radius $\\delta$ with constant $\\eta$. Then for every $h\\in X$ with $\\|h\\|_X\\le\\delta$,\n\n$$\n(1-\\eta)\\,\\|F(x+h)-F(x)\\|_Y\\le\\|F'(x)h\\|_Y\\le(1+\\eta)\\,\\|F(x+h)-F(x)\\|_Y.\n$$"
    ],
    "thm-ip-tcc-local-minimum-norm-identifiability": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $X,Y$ be real Hilbert spaces, let $U\\subseteq X$ be open, and let $F:U\\to Y$ be Fréchet differentiable. Let $x_0\\in X$, $y\\in Y$, and let $x^\\dagger\\in U$ be an $x_0$-minimum-norm solution of $F(x)=y$ on $U$. Suppose that for some $\\delta>0$ the closed ball $\\overline B_\\delta(x^\\dagger)$ lies in $U$, the local tangential cone condition holds at $x^\\dagger$ on radius $\\delta$ with a constant $0\\le\\eta<1$, and\n\n$$x^\\dagger-x_0\\in\\ker(F'(x^\\dagger))^\\perp.$$\n\nThen every $x\\in\\overline B_\\delta(x^\\dagger)$ with $F(x)=y$ and $x\\ne x^\\dagger$ satisfies\n\n$$\\|x-x_0\\|_X>\\|x^\\dagger-x_0\\|_X.$$\n\nConsequently, $x^\\dagger$ is the unique $x_0$-minimum-norm solution among the exact solutions in $\\overline B_\\delta(x^\\dagger)$."
    ],
